plan.approach:
Capture-and-compose, the winner for 2 of the 3 judges. Dota itself renders every HUD pixel. The browser only composites per-channel mattes, in the blend space measured from the captures, over a world captured in the same paused moment. Hybrid's robustness ideas are grafted in, and every flaw the judges raised is fixed and re-checked against the Valve sources in assets/dota-hud/panorama and the 2004-file Valve CSS dump.

One sitting covers everything: C1 (the main pack, about 6 minutes of automatic F12) and C2 (acceptance, about 1 minute). Pre-built fallback packs (F-bg, F-scale×5, F-chat) sit in the same download. A hosted PowerShell watcher reads each screenshot live and starts a fallback only if a mechanism failed.

**What changes compared with the three designs:**

**1. A region's fast state and its backdrop sit on the same panel, so they share one clock.** #lower_hud carries:
- its own background-color: a local K/W/G/T backdrop under the whole lower HUD, with the minimap lifted to z-index 3 so it is painted over that backdrop;
- ui-scale;
- a 6-px box-shadow ring used as a marker. Its colour encodes the block and core/guard part (R=255, G=20·block, B=0/120/240). Its screen height encodes the scale.
- opacity, for the "hidden" windows.

Scale and backdrop therefore cannot drift apart. No design relies on two panels' animation clocks agreeing.

**2. Slower toggles live on child panels and are held long enough.** #center_bg opacity, the flares and the inset strips are held for whole blocks with a guard scale on each side. Any child-clock offset up to ±3 s loses nothing. #AbilityBevel is built when the hero spawns, so it runs its own 48-s on/off clock and is classified per slot from pixels.

**3. The top bar, chat and the remaining panels are matted over a fast global backdrop.** #HUDElements background-color cycles K, W, T at 1.5 s per slot. Any 3 consecutive slots contain a K and a W, so the ≥6-s holds of these regions yield K/W frames at any clock offset.

**4. Properties Valve never animates in keyframes are isolated.** ui-scale, font-size and height (0 uses in Valve @keyframes, but present in transition-property) each get their own animation. Valve uses comma lists too (crownfall shmup: animation-name/duration/timing lists), so one failure cannot take the others down. visibility, horizontal-align, width and y are never animated.

**5. Chat is fixed.** The capture chat.css deletes exactly three Valve font-size declarations:
- `.ChatTarget` 14px (line 830);
- `DOTAChat#HudChat .ChatTarget` 18px (line 1325);
- `DOTAChat#HudChat .GameAllChat/.GameAlliesChat/…` 18px (line 1495).

The target and message spans then inherit the animated line size, exactly as production's explicit rules set them. All lines restart their 13-font cycle together when the chat input closes, via `DOTAChat#HudChat:not(.Active) .ChatLine`. No chat.xml override.

**6. The wash law and opacity model are fitted on a clone.** #arcana_container is styled exactly like #center_bg (#1620346c + ability_bg_psd) and placed over the world. #center_bg therefore never carries an animated wash in C1. Production's static wash is then proven on the real panel in C2.

**7. The world comes without #HUDElements opacity.** Each region has a hidden window (lower, top, chat, rest). Those windows plus global T frames give the world. The cursor is removed exactly: the owner parks it at A, then at B.

**8. Colour-blind mode is captured both ways.** The owner flips «Режим цветовой слепоты» once mid-run. The site defaults to Valve's green; a toggle shows the owner's blue.

**9. C2 runs the exact production hudRules() for one complex setting plus only the backdrop.** It proves:
- visibility:collapse is the same as opacity 0;
- static ui-scale is the same as animated, at 85 and 110;
- the wash law on the real panel;
- chat at 400 px / 22 px / 50 % background, centred;
- no visible change for statue and teamItems.

**10. The watcher is simulated.** A coverage simulator over 3000 random clock offsets (child ±3 s, minimap ±30 s, spawn clock arbitrary, 45–70 s gap for the colour-blind flip) completes C1 in 100 % of trials with the watcher's stop rule. Median: about 356 s wall, about 410 frames.

**Artefacts in /tmp/claude-0/-home-code-gridstudio/393fe78e-42d4-4fe6-823d-d9629de18d4f/scratchpad/design/final/:**
- plan.mjs: tracks;
- gen.mjs: CSS generator with self-checks;
- simad2.mjs: coverage simulator;
- chatcss.mjs: chat.css edit;
- out/*.css and out/*.min.css (md5 c1 212ddb0e…, c2 7ccc90d5…);
- out/plan.json.

**Effort:** about 8–9 dev-days for the HUD; the menu adds about 4–5.

captures.purpose:
Main capture. It produces exact per-channel mattes of:
- the lower HUD + minimap at lower ui-scale 100/95/90/85/80/75/70, in four toggle states each: H1 (center_bg on, flares/insets on), A1 (center_bg off), A0 (all off), H0 (center_bg on, flares/insets off);
- bevel on/off per slot;
- lower K/W/G plus the local G at every scale (blend-space test and the K/G fallback).

It also captures:
- **Real views over the world:** RDEF (default), RCLR (opacity .35, flares/insets off) and RCMP (opacity .70, flares off, lower 85).
- **Top bar** at 11 scales (70–120) × DayGlow 0.1/0.3.
- **Chat:** the owner's 3 typed lines at fonts 14–26, the chat mask at 162/250/100 px, and the hidden box.
- **Rest** (quick stats, menu buttons).
- **Wash/opacity calibration clone:** 6 washes, plus .35 and .55 opacity.
- **World:** from every region's hidden window plus global T, cursor at A and at B, both colour-blind states.

Built-in verification:
- **Plates:** region hidden + global K/W gives a pixel-exact K/W screen, which proves the backdrop covers the world.
- **Per-pixel G consistency** proves the HUD is drawn over the backdrop with affine blends.

Live probes report whether ui-scale, font-size and height animate.

Timeline:
- global K/W/T at 1.5 s each;
- lower cycle 178.5 s (119 slots);
- top 138 s; DayGlow 12 s;
- font 97.5 s; chat box 118.5 s;
- bevel 48 s; wash clone 54 s;
- rest hidden 6 s per 60 s.

