Ingest. Unzip, then:
- keep only 8-bit RGB 1920×1080 PNGs; refuse JPG;
- read session.json: the watcher's F12 log, phase 1/2 boundaries, the colour-blind gap, live verdicts, which fallback packs ran;
- decode with sharp to raw RGB and group frames by pack (C1, C2, F-*).

Temporal stability. For each (region, state, backdrop) group take the per-pixel median. Pixels that vary inside a group are flagged: particles animating during pause, possible portrait idle. For these:
- base = per-pixel minimum over the group's K frames;
- overlay = one representative K frame minus that base (additive);
- opaque engine panels (3D portrait, minimap) use b = P_K where P_K = P_W.

Mattes, per channel, in φ:
- b = φ(P_K), a = φ(P_W) − φ(P_K);
- where W clips (additive glow), use K/G instead: a = (φ(P_G) − b) / φ(g);
- per-channel a keeps LCD/subpixel text fringes and screen-blend pixels exact;
- gate: every HON G frame must be reproduced within ±1.

Region layers:
- **Lower:** per scale 100…70, the states H1, A1, A0 and H0 from local-backdrop frames, the minimap included. Per-slot bevel on/off patches. Colour-blind patches.
- **Top:** per scale 70…120, two layers (DayGlow 0.1 and 0.3), plus colour-blind patches.
- **Rest:** one static layer from global K/W.
- **Chat:**
  - line strips per line and font, L = strip / mask162(y), since lines sit in the unfaded bottom of the box;
  - line pitch per font;
  - box anchor: bottom = chat bottom − controls height;
  - the lines panel's left offset;
  - the opacity-mask profile per height: 162, 250 and 100 from C1, and 400 or Valve's squish from C2.
- **Wash clone:** 9 mattes.
- **World, one per colour-blind phase:**
  - pixels outside every region come from global-T frames;
  - pixels under each region come from that region's hidden-window frames with global T;
  - the cursor box at A is taken from phase-2 frames and the box at B from phase-1 frames;
  - ring rows and the clone rectangle come from hidden-region frames.

Export to assets/dota-hud/capture/:
- manifest.json: φ, laws, scale sets, zones, chat model, colour-blind patches, DayGlow pulse;
- per layer a pair <layer>.b.webp and <layer>.a.webp: lossless WebP, 3-channel (no alpha, so no premultiply), cropped; variants stored as 64×64 tile patches over their base;
- world-cb0.webp and world-cb1.webp, lossless;
- checksums.

After acceptance, delete the raw frames from the server and the capture packs from dev hosting.

implementation:
tools/hud-capture/gs-hud-capture.ps1, hosted. A C# helper compiled with Add-Type does the pixel probes.
- **Setup:**
  - find Dota through the SteamPath registry key and libraryfolders.vdf, reusing the scripts/installer.mjs logic;
  - refuse while dota2.exe runs;
  - restore any leftover .gs-backup first;
  - back up pak03; download each pack and check its SHA-256;
  - ask for or create C:\\GSShots.
- **Start:** wait for dota2.exe and the owner's first F12. Validate that the PNG is 1920×1080 and the pack is active (ring present, or exact K/W at the free points).
- **Auto mode:** every 0.75 s, only while dota2.exe is the foreground window, send F12 with SendInput (VK 0x7B, scan 0x58). Copy new PNGs to Desktop\\gs-hud-capture\\C1_####.png and so on.
- **Live verdicts after about 60 s:**
  - backdrop exact;
  - ring found;
  - lower ui-scale animating (ring row takes at least 3 values);
  - top ui-scale animating (probes (600,12), (1360,12), (1400,12) over K);
  - chat font animating (ink extent in x 40..840, y 200..445 changes by at least 10 px);
  - wash clone changing.
- **Phase control:**
  - phase 1 lasts at least 145 s, then a double beep and auto mode pauses until the owner presses F12;
  - phase 2 lasts at least 145 s and runs until every lower core slot has been seen with its local backdrop, and each real block with global K, W and T;
  - then a triple beep.
- **Next steps:** queue F-bg, F-scale×5 or F-chat according to the verdicts, then C2 (60–75 s, at least 3 K/W/T frames and at least 2 hidden-T frames).
- **Finish:** restore pak03 (also inside try/finally), write session.json, zip with store compression to Desktop\\gs-hud-capture.zip, open https://0807.st.

src/customize/panorama/hud-compose.mjs: a pure compose(manifest, layers, settings, world) on typed arrays with a φ LUT.
- Settings map straight from hudSettings():
  - opacity → t;
  - tint and strength → the wash, exactly as hudRules writes it;
  - hide keys → zone states;
  - lower/top → scale level;
  - chat → geometry, mask and background.
- The solver, the tests and the page all share it.
- hud-compose.worker.js renders through OffscreenCanvas, so slider drags stay off the main thread.

per_setting.chat:
The three lines the owner types (allies 'го рошан', all 'gg wp', allies 'нужна мана') are the game's own pixels at every font 14–26: persona at Valve's 20 px, target, hero icon, shadow. The C1 chat.css edit lets the target and message spans inherit the animated line size, which equals production's explicit rule.

Placement is a measured model:
- #ChatMainPanel is bottom-anchored with flow-children down, so the box grows upward from the bottom: chat bottom − controls height;
- left, centre or right with Valve-style 24-px margins;
- y as px;
- line pitch per font;
- the opacity-mask profile is the stretched 3×239 hudchat_mask, fitted on 100/162/250 (C1) and 400 (C2);
- the background is #000 with alpha round(back·2.55), composited in φ;
- chat is drawn above the top bar and under the rest/lower HUD, following Valve's child order.

Chat width is snapped to step 10 so a centred chat stays on whole pixels. If C2 shows Panorama squishing a box above 162 px inside the 460-px chat, the preview reproduces it.

Limits:
- the lines are the owner's own, with his nickname and guild tag, RU only;
- other texts would need another short capture;
- with the F-chat fallback, fonts are exact at even sizes only.
